                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s17IHA" type="apodous"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>وَاعْلَمُوْا أَمَّمَا غَنَمْتُمْ مِّنْ شَئًْ فَأَنَّ لِلهِ خُمْسَهُ ولِلرَّسُوْلِ وَلَِذِى الْقُرْبَى </incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#19v">-19v</locus>قَدْ نَبَّأَنَا اَللَهُ مِنْ أَخْبَارِكُمْ وِسَيَرَي الله عَمَلَكُمْ \ ورسوله<note>The last word is the catchword. </note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>First word of the guz' rubricated, red ink. Words left incomplete at the end of lines and rewritten in full on the following line on almost all folios. Some words completed on the following line. Deletions (ff.9r-v, 13r, 14v, 15v, 19v). Catchwords, some penciled. F.20r was restored. The text ends abruptly in the middle of verse 9:94 (surat al-Tawba). The first word (yaʻtadirūna) is written in larger hand and traced with red. It indicates the beginning of ǧuz' 11,</note>
                     <note/>
                  </msItem>
